{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago","id":1516376,"title":"New Orleans or Chicago?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2023-06-27T16:47:55-07:00","id":1516376,"title":"New Orleans or Chicago?","content":"I am hoping in a few months to run a VtR 1e game set in either New Orleans or Chicago. Any suggestions as to which one would be the better setting to use?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:10:30-07:00","id":1516381,"title":"","content":"Depends on a number of factors.<br /> <br /> 1) Are you using the settings as they are in the books, or are you just inclined to the locales?<br /> 2) If you're using the settings, which themes and set pieces do you think your play group would prefer to play with?<br /> 3) If you're just using the locales, what aesthetics/geography/trade/politics/etc. do you think would draw your players in?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:32:01-07:00","id":1516386,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago#post1516376\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am hoping in a few months to run a VtR 1e game set in either New Orleans or Chicago. Any suggestions as to which one would be the better setting to use?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, what are you looking for in a city in the first place? It could be Chicago, New Orleans, a mish-mash of NPC archetypes and concepts from Damnation City and/or Covenantbooks....<br /> Back almost ten years ago when a friend decided to run a game set in Rio de Janeiro he made about a dozen major NPCs, to which we then added another half-dozen between our PCs' (who were supposed to be 80-120 years into unlife ancillae) childer and some close associates.<br /> <br /> Later on for a number of reasons he passed the baton as ST to me and i'm not gonna lie, while i proceeded to make a bunch of kindred big or small for the city, about 2/3 of them were characters from either 1e VtR core or VtM: Bloodlines that i would then kitbash into something else with my picks of clan, bloodline and/or covenant, with some historical highlight and new NPC connections mixed in.<br /> <br /> For a quick &amp; dirty example - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Natasha_Preston\" target=\"_blank\">Natasha Preston</a> from the corebook became Natasha Prestes, secretary to the Invictus Primogen.<br /> But she's also my little expy of sorts for the <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Therese_Voerman\" target=\"_blank\">Voerman</a> sisters, meaning she also plans of becoming a nightclub owner as a path to greater influence and a &quot;problem sister&quot;\u200b that happens to be involved with the Carthians.<br /> But for a little extra twist, they are two souls vying for the same body and neither of them knows which twin was a ghost first anymore - also <a href=\"http://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dragolescu\" target=\"_blank\">the reason</a> their twisted <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Maximillian_Strauss\" target=\"_blank\">sire</a> would pick them for childer.<br /> <br /> Final results can sometimes look nearly unrecognizable from their sources depending on what you feel like adding to the mix, might be said<br /> It's all up to what your interests and objectives with the game are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-27-2023, 08:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T17:45:37-07:00","id":1516390,"title":"","content":"I enjoy running political vampire stories in Masquerade. With Requiem I'm hoping to lean into a more horror and mystery direction. I like using the city books as is generally, adding new ideas where needed. I'd also like to use the city book to explore the covenants in more detail. My group tried VtR when it first came out but it never really grabbed them setting wise after years of playing VtM. I had moved out of the area back then so never got the chance to try VtR but would like to now that I've reconnected with my old group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T18:39:44-07:00","id":1516399,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516390#post1516390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I enjoy running political vampire stories in Masquerade. With Requiem I'm hoping to lean into a more horror and mystery direction. I like using the city books as is generally, adding new ideas where needed. I'd also like to use the city book to explore the covenants in more detail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Both are good books imho and should be equally entertaining for intrigue and horror - New Orleans did get a free introductory scenario/story arc, <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/1459/Vampire-The-Requiem-Demo-Full?src=also_purchased\" target=\"_blank\">Mary's Child</a>, while the Chicago book has more crossover elements with info on Uratha and Awakened, what can definitely provide for some extra bits to mine for certain kinds of mystery as such. Either or both might be fun and of use for you.<br /> <br /> Plus, there's always room for adaptation and customization - one of the reasons i stole some of the New Orleans NPCs for my version of Rio de Janeiro is because i found the themes of ethnic and religious tensions mixed in with matters of covenant and their leading elders quite resonant with a number of common issues to Rio and many other urban centers in Brasil too.<br /> <br /> (Not to mention i definitely did not stop there...<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516390#post1516390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My group tried VtR when it first came out but it never really grabbed them setting wise after years of playing VtM. I had moved out of the area back then so never got the chance to try VtR but would like to now that I've reconnected with my old group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now <b>that</b> is very important - what grabbed you on Requiem as a setting and what are your thoughts on why it didn't quite work for them? Having a good idea beforehand and how to perhaps deal with it, making the game more appealing or resonant to your old group this time around definitely matters, imho.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-27-2023, 09:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T19:02:05-07:00","id":1516401,"title":"","content":"I was always invested in VtM's history/lore and metaplot. V5, aside from the OP books was not my cup of tea setting wise. I also didn't appreciate a lot of the rules changes. Requiem's toolkit approach setting wise is intriguing. The horror/mystery aspect is a nice change of pace, especially when incorporating the blue books. The rules changes that I didn't care for in V5 don't bother me so much in Requiem, especially with the toolkit approach. I enjoy looking through Danse Macabre for ideas. As for my group, I think when VtR first came out it felt fairly generic to them after Masquerade. Hopefully I and they will enjoy it more this time around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T19:21:07-07:00","id":1516404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516401#post1516401\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I was always invested in VtM's history/lore and metaplot. V5, aside from the OP books was not my cup of tea setting wise. I also didn't appreciate a lot of the rules changes. Requiem's toolkit approach setting wise is intriguing. The horror/mystery aspect is a nice change of pace, especially when incorporating the blue books. The rules changes that I didn't care for in V5 don't bother me so much in Requiem, especially with the toolkit approach. I enjoy looking through Danse Macabre for ideas. As for my group, I think when VtR first came out it felt fairly generic to them after Masquerade. Hopefully I and they will enjoy it more this time around.</div> </div> </div> </div>What other Requiem books do you have beside the 1e Core and Danse Macabre? Covenant and Clanbooks are a must i'd say and i would also strongly reccomend Mythologies and Night Horrors: Wicked Dead for some extra bits to &quot;hack the setting&quot; with (Mirrors too, though that one is more of a blue book).<br /> <br /> Ancient Mysteries and Requiem for Rome + Fall of the Camarilla can also be quite useful as springboards for some worldbuilding across the ages. The Dark Eras series, though geared toward 2nd edition, also covers that niche/spot wonderfully i dare say.<br /> <br /> And speaking of Rome... are you familiar with the Strix? If you are, what are your opinions on them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-27T19:37:29-07:00","id":1516405,"title":"","content":"I have the entire line of 1ed CofD books, although I've mostly only read the blue books and VtR ones. I really enjoyed Mythologies back in the day. I have picked up the 2e corebook along with SotC and 1000 years. I am familiar with the Strix. I like idea of them. One thing I really appreciate in VtR is there is more interaction with spirits and their worlds. I recall reading how vampires could wander the realm of the dead while in torpor. Could definitely see an interaction with a Strix there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T10:02:05-07:00","id":1516475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516405#post1516405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have the entire line of 1ed CofD books, although I've mostly only read the blue books and VtR ones. I really enjoyed Mythologies back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mythologies is a great book that keeps on giving when it comes to concepts to twist kindred existence in all sorts of <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1316770-ever-ran-a-game-using-danse-macabre-content?p=1326463#post1326463\">bizarre directions</a> - it's one of my three favorite and most used Requiem books alongside Night Horrors: Wicked Dead and Danse Macabre.<br /> <br /> Well, if you already have all 1ed books i'd encourage you to take some time to peek on Chicago and New Orleans both to see which one gets your fancy the most, or canibalize fragments from both or other books like Shadows of Mexico, UK, Boston Unveiled or others to craft your own mysterious metropolis of sorts. Not to mention that one's choice of city can on itself bring all sorts of ideas.<br /> <br /> Case in point, when we started working on Rio de Janeiro for our chronicle, i decided to mine some historical flashpoints and bits of brazilian folklore in composing my character. This led for example to the idea of local Morbus were/are infamous for a controversial association with a cult dedicated to both the orisha <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Babal%C3%BA-Ay%C3%A9\" target=\"_blank\">Omolu</a>, <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lazarus_of_Bethany#Lazarus_as_Babalu_Aye_in_Santer%C3%ADa\" target=\"_blank\">Saint Lazarus</a> and <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Four_Horsemen_of_the_Apocalypse#As_infectious_disease\" target=\"_blank\">Pestilence</a>, periodically spreading epidemics through the city until a prince made their containment into a rallying point for local kindred of many covenants, leading to their (apparent) extinction during the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vaccine_Revolt\" target=\"_blank\">early 20th century</a> - conflict that my PC as a back then recently arrived neonate got really involved with as one of the Sheriff's hounds, due to his capacity to see and communicate with the ghosts of those killed by kindred. Not a matter of &quot;vampires manipulate everything&quot; but of how kindred will be moved along with the situation around them or piggyback on already existing tensions for their benefit like the parasites they are. It also meshes NPCs and events very well with the city and what themes you feel like exploring.<br /> <br /> Another fun highlight was the &quot;crias de chumbo&quot; (childer of lead, a reference to the &quot;years of lead&quot;, the harshest period of political persecution under military dictatorship between the 60s to 80s in Brasil) a clique/social circle of sorts beyond their family or covenant relations, a generation of kindred spawned from artists, intellectuals, university students or young people of the period &quot;disappeared with&quot; by the military dictatorship, for connections (factual or spurious) with the armed resistance movements.<br /> <br /> In particular, prisioners in interrogation centers of the DOPS (the political police of the military junta) who would be rescued - and mass embraced - by the formation of rescue posse of several Dragons, Carthians and kindred in other covenants or unaligned, angry and frustrated with how the military's &quot;witch hunts&quot; among intellectual and student circles were messing with the herds and prospective childer of a number of them.<br /> <br /> As one can imagine, about two dozen angry kindred of varied ages with a score to settle with a secret police far from aware of them was not a pretty sight to see, at all. Specially when they decide to embrace any and all prisioners and let the hungry childer slake their thirst for blood and vengeance both.<br /> <br /> Eventually\u200b the prince of the time would manage to get things under wraps once more and calm the resulting tensions between Invictus (strongly associated with the military) and everybody else, but the particularities of the incident would create a sort of unique rapport beyond lineage or faction between many childer of this era in the city alongside the nickname.<br /> <br /> <br /> But anyway, the choice of city can on itself lead to all kinds of possible inspiration that go far beyond the book proper. <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Prince_of_100,000_Leaves\" target=\"_blank\">This</a> for example, can work wonderfully as a source of wonder &amp; horror in any one game with little to no necessity of anything else from either the sourcebook or the city of Boston proper.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516405#post1516405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have picked up the 2e corebook along with SotC and 1000 years. I am familiar with the Strix. I like idea of them. One thing I really appreciate in VtR is there is more interaction with spirits and their worlds. I recall reading how vampires could wander the realm of the dead while in torpor. Could definitely see an interaction with a Strix there.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> SotC? Sorry, not clicking which book you're talking about. Do you have any plans for the Strix, as either a background/worldbuiling element or an actual thing the PCs might have to interact, confront or deal with?<br /> <br /> Either way is good and fine - in the aforementioned chronicle, me and the previous ST kind of zig-zagged with this: the strix per se never, ever made an appearance, at most one PC came across a mausoleum with clear owl imagery kept by a Ventrue elder &amp; his descendants, that they would periodically visit for some sort of ceremonies every time a new individual was added to the brood or rumours of one's destruction started to spread. After a few nights of snooping around, the player (also a Ventrue) decided to leave the mausoleum alone - and in fact choose to set up a few extra security measures to guard the place, just in case. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> But <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1340546-are-the-strix-still-a-focus?p=1340808#post1340808\">no strix </a>around not exactly means their brand of tricks and ploys could not appear in <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1329973-is-the-unholy-claimed?p=1339443#post1339443\">other</a>, unexpected <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1340546-are-the-strix-still-a-focus?p=1341117#post1341117\">guises</a>. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T14:13:26-07:00","id":1516526,"title":"","content":"I have (in PDF, mind) the 1E Covenant books and the 2E book Secrets of the Covenants. The fiction part of SotC for the Lancea Sanctum was about how hard Prince Vidal was affected by Hurricane Katrina and the after effects, which include an influx of Carthians from Houston.<br /> <br /> So if you set it in New Orleans, likely conflicts would include Sanctified fighting Carthians or Sanctified fighting Sanctified, especially if you lean into the implications that Vidal was set to go full <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom%C3%A1s_de_Torquemada\" target=\"_blank\">Torquemada</a>...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3201-father-enoch","name":"Father Enoch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3201_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"285"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T17:28:34-07:00","id":1516557,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Father Enoch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516526#post1516526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have (in PDF, mind) the 1E Covenant books and the 2E book Secrets of the Covenants. The fiction part of SotC for the Lancea Sanctum was about how hard Prince Vidal was affected by Hurricane Katrina and the after effects, which include an influx of Carthians from Houston.<br /> <br /> So if you set it in New Orleans, likely conflicts would include Sanctified fighting Carthians or Sanctified fighting Sanctified, especially if you lean into the implications that Vidal was set to go full <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tom%C3%A1s_de_Torquemada\" target=\"_blank\">Torquemada</a>...</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, Secrets of the Covenants, that' what the OP meant with SotC, thanks Enoch - good point on the reference to post-Katrina references to New Orleans in the book, the Mekhet clanbook is another one where one may find some more in the form of a number of letters sent by a 19th century Morbus awakened in the hurricane's aftermath to Frances.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't doubt there being some other references to either New Orleans or Chicago peppered amidst the clanbooks in the form of fiction we are forgetting about.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516405#post1516405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing I really appreciate in VtR is there is more interaction with spirits and their worlds. I recall reading how vampires could wander the realm of the dead while in torpor. Could definitely see an interaction with a Strix there.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200b<br /> <br /> That is .... dubious. Mythologies has a section called &quot;the Second Death&quot;, that in contrast to the &quot;Understanding the Fog of Eternity&quot; sub-chapter about Torpor as a journey through dream vistas and twisted memory, focuses on the idea of Torpor as a dive into some sort of realm of dead and while not outright stated, there are some definite similarities to a number of things described in <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Book_of_the_Dead\" target=\"_blank\">Book of the Dead</a>, so while mentioned, it clearly sits in the &quot;barely explored options&quot; camp.<br /> <br /> That said, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1472918-vampire-otherworld?p=1473170#post1473170\">the subject </a>is something i have <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1316770-ever-ran-a-game-using-danse-macabre-content?p=1326463#post1326463\">tinkered</a> with and rambled on <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1493349-now-available-on-stv-bloodlines-the-ageless?p=1493882#post1493882\">more than once</a>. Much like i have toyed with things <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1329973-is-the-unholy-claimed/page2#post1340427\">like the Strix</a>\u200b and yet <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1461345-crazy-ideas-what-would-you-want-out-of-a-3ed-of-requiem?p=1462264#post1462264\">not</a>.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 06-28-2023, 08:43 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T18:59:23-07:00","id":1516581,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3761\" data-vbnamecard=\"3761\">Yab</a>, any concepts, hooks or story beats from either your previous attempt at VtR or past VtM games you'd be interested in trying once more or exploring in different ways this time around?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:10:58-07:00","id":1516586,"title":"","content":"Baaldam,<br /> Your last 2 posts for some reason are only appearing to me via My Recent Posts tool in my profile, they are highlighted as green and unapproved for some reason. I am not seeing them in the thread in the forum. That being said, I do intend to read both city books plus Boston Unveiled. That was an intriguing link you posted. The Boston area is where I'm originally from. Would be more work to adapt it for a 3 in 1 setting like the Chicago book but certainly interesting. <br /> <br /> As for the torpor idea, I have always liked the idea that kindred souls were somehow accessing the world of the dead or a sub-realm of it in some fashion while in torpor since reading Mythologies years ago. It would be a nice way to let a PC to continue to play if they were to get knocked into torpor unexpectedly during a session.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T19:24:44-07:00","id":1516590,"title":"","content":"Baaldam, I am interested in eventually incorporating the other gamelines into whichever city I base the game in. I am more interested in exploring the horror/mystery/occult concepts with VtR. When I ran VtM previously my focus was more on political conflict. My last VtM game I attempted to explore the history of Chicago by running flashback storylines between the 1860s and the 2020s. But I have no doubt I will return to political conflict at some point in a Requiem game.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T20:09:01-07:00","id":1516600,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516590#post1516590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baaldam, I am interested in eventually incorporating the other gamelines into whichever city I base the game in. I am more interested in exploring the horror/mystery/occult concepts with VtR. When I ran VtM previously my focus was more on political conflict. My last VtM game I attempted to explore the history of Chicago by running flashback storylines between the 1860s and the 2020s. But I have no doubt I will return to political conflict at some point in a Requiem game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmm, from the &quot;horror/mystery/occult concepts&quot; perspective, i'd say New Orleans is possibly the more convenient place with its pop culture association with voodoo and the ongoing conflicts between both LS &amp; Crone and internal subdivisions within the local brands of both covenants, though the crossover elements of the Chicago book could compensate somewhat for that. Though it's far from a deal-breaker either way - not like one can't mine lots of weirdness and mystery to tinker with from either the blue books or demo adventures for each of the game lines among other bits.<br /> <br /> Chicago as a book touches on a place that you already made a VtM game for the same group in the past. It could be a bother due to generating misplaced expectations or unwelcome comparisons or be interesting exactly to provide contrast and subvert some good/bad expectations based on the previous game.<br /> <br /> As an aside, what city do you and your group live on, if you don't mind me asking?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-28T20:41:48-07:00","id":1516604,"title":"","content":"With New Orlean's reputation for hauntings and the Louisiana folklore of the rougarou, New Orleans has ready built hooks for Geist and Werewolf crossovers, besides the existing Vampire material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/27841-haintbleu","name":"HaintBleu","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2023"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T11:04:55-07:00","id":1516671,"title":"","content":"Baaldam, most of my group live in Rhode Island, around Providence. Another player is in Houston, another in DC, and I live in Delaware these days. We mostly play over zoom.<br /> <br /> I think right now I'm leaning towards New Orleans. I've visited the city a few times, and it would be fun to eventually run a game in each of the big 3 setting books (Rockies, Boston, etc...).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T19:12:31-07:00","id":1516719,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516671#post1516671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Baaldam, most of my group live in Rhode Island, around Providence. Another player is in Houston, another in DC, and I live in Delaware these days. We mostly play over zoom.</div> </div> </div> </div>Providence?!?!?! You guys come from the darkest eldritch heart of the <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lovecraft_Country\" target=\"_blank\">Lovecraft Country</a> - no, not <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=eEvK1Zwi9XY\" target=\"_blank\">that one</a> - and we are talking &quot;New Orleans or Chicago&quot;? WHY.......<br /> <br /> Sorry, couldn't resist. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516671#post1516671\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think right now I'm leaning towards New Orleans. I've visited the city a few times, and it would be fun to eventually run a game in each of the big 3 setting books (Rockies, Boston, etc...).</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bOh yeah, the city does bring to mind some real <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=0iKzekw3xn8\" target=\"_blank\">classics</a> indeed.<br /> <br /> About going through the big setting book regions - ever considered a game with <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Nomads_(book)\" target=\"_blank\">Nomads</a> elements? Either way, playing with some of the SAS adventures can certainly provide some easy to adapt and use entry points for them. Or coming up with your own crazy bits of storylines. This <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Ruins_of_Ur\" target=\"_blank\">one</a>, though made as simply a teaser of sorts for <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/World_of_Darkness:_Dogs_of_War\" target=\"_blank\">a certain blue book</a>, would serve as major inspiration in completety retooling one of the flashpoints from Ancient Mysteries into my own almost book-sized period setting of sorts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T20:28:59-07:00","id":1516725,"title":"","content":"Yeah, we've certainly explored Providence many times in our games LOL. I have always had a soft spot for New Orleans and Chicago since I ran my earliest VtM games there. I always wanted to do a Nomads Sabbat game, incorporating the clan novels crusades and bouncing back and forth between Montreal and Mexico City. I will look into the SAS for ideas. What setting are you developing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-29T21:56:53-07:00","id":1516733,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516725#post1516725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, we've certainly explored Providence many times in our games LOL. I have always had a soft spot for New Orleans and Chicago since I ran my earliest VtM games there. I always wanted to do a Nomads Sabbat game, incorporating the clan novels crusades and bouncing back and forth between Montreal and Mexico City. I will look into the SAS for ideas. What setting are you developing?</div> </div> </div> </div>At the present i'm messing more with VtM due to new Discord game group circunstances (setting is V20 with some Redemption, Bloodlines, the Winter's Teeth V5 comic books mashup, bonkers stuff involving a Salubri warrior-nun out of torpor, a Gangrel who claims to be an &quot;ex-Gargoyle&quot; cured by Caine in LA, the fledgling from Bloodlines as a Cappadocian, a mad thot goth with an evil magical sword who claims to be Dracula's bride, a Toreador of partial native american descent that researchs &quot;Drowned Legacies&quot; and the Caitiff noddist better known as german rapper DJ Lestat who manages to somehow keep this crowd of yahoos together under the same roof as his tour bus globetrotts across the world with the raves as cover for a Gehenna cult connected to the &quot;<a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Beckett&#39;s_Jyhad_Diary#False_Caine\" target=\"_blank\">False Caine</a>&quot; incidents)<br /> <br /> <br /> Almost a decade ago i alternated ST duties with two other friends in a Requiem chronicle set in Rio de Janeiro, opportunity that i used to mix a lot of brazilian history and folklore with elements taken from Mythologies, Wicked Dead, Danse Macabre and a bunch of other books, Requiem and not - astral journeys and interactions with goetic demons through Torpor, strange rituals involving mirrors, dreams, lacrima (bloody sap of mandragora ghoul plants) consumption, deals with the reaper spirits or more to open passages to obscure realms of existence, covens of not kindred blood witches, clans of shapeshifters who hunt the dead &quot;to return them to the sacred tree fields&quot;, heretic Morbus cults that blur the lines between Sanctum &amp; Crone and nearly sparked a zombie apocalypse in the city (&quot;nearly&quot; in the sense that a good chunk of a whole district's population was turned to ash to contain the crisis and masquerade breach, barely), an isle cordoned off for decades due to an UFO suicide cult bringing <i>something</i> with their actions and much more besides.<br /> <br /> Not related, but also did a bunch of &quot;historical horror&quot; short story arcs that half the time had more in common Glen Cook's Black Company or Bran Mak Morn stories than your average Rome episode. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />\u200b","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T15:54:16-07:00","id":1516830,"title":"","content":"Does the goth have the Sword of Nul? I worked that into my old Chicago game. The Rio chronicle sounds interesting. Mirrors have been an interesting concept in the NWoD books.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T19:06:17-07:00","id":1516852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516830#post1516830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the goth have the Sword of Nul? I worked that into my old Chicago game.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yessss, exactly that one. Bela now wields the sword, just like <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Bela\" target=\"_blank\">her sire</a>, once did. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> One thing i've expanded upon is the idea that the demon can affect the sword's wielder, causing visions, nightmares and such - in our chronicle i used that to do a session where most of the coterie (issues of when one two many PCs decide to have Auspex 3+ and to mess with either blade or its wielder) dove headfirst alongside Bela into the messy and atrocious mindscape of Tiamat.<br /> The first but most probably not the last time they'll interact with her past and divided self.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516830#post1516830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Rio chronicle sounds interesting. Mirrors have been an interesting concept in the NWoD books.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was loads of fun indeed, both to play and to ST at turns.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-06-30T20:18:19-07:00","id":1516855,"title":"","content":"I used the Sword as part of the final story in my first Chicago game. My PCs had to deal with one of them being the new host of Dragonskyr. I always appreciated Diablerie Britain's impact on early VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T07:43:05-07:00","id":1516890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Yab</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516855#post1516855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I used the Sword as part of the final story in my first Chicago game. My PCs had to deal with one of them being the new host of Dragonskyr. I always appreciated Diablerie Britain's impact on early VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Sword in my game serves as both MacGuffin - <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Dylan_Bruce?#V20_Timeline\" target=\"_blank\">Dylan Bruce</a>, who happens to descend from Tiamat has become aware of the connection and see it as &quot;his rightful heirloom&quot; - and also a plot device dealing with the complete absence of buildup, hints or sort of connection between Tiamat's past and her divided true nature in Diablerie: Britain as written. Through the dreams &amp; visions the PCs get to interact with both Lan-Tula (the woman behind the monster) and Dura-kon-sikir the demon in surreal, fractured form and maybe catch on the signs there's more at stake than destroying/consuming a demented ancient. <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=22gw_64AGKM\" target=\"_blank\">The Cell</a> has been something of an <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=nCuYBELZjpY\" target=\"_blank\">inspiration</a> in that &quot;dreamdelve&quot; subplot/minigame of sorts.<br /> <br /> (Also tweaked the names a bit in a vain attempt to make them sound somewhat more summerian at least)\u200b<br /> <br /> One major bit of crypto-lore that i have added is that Tiamat being among the many elusive figures called <a href=\"https://whitewolf.fandom.com/wiki/Shaitan\" target=\"_blank\">Shaitan</a> by through the ages of kindred history, making Dylan's supposed descent and infernalist ties quite a big deal indeed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-01-2023, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T17:32:37-07:00","id":1516931,"title":"","content":"I like the new names, as well as the use of Dylan and Shaitan.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-01T17:53:45-07:00","id":1516933,"title":"","content":"Why not both? <br /> <br /> Either have a character-tree, in which, there are two simultaneous games in each city, with a related plot one another or, have the vampires spend winter in New Orleans and summers in Chicago and the vampires travel back and forth in the Fall and Spring.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;I have all the power in the world to give you, and all you have to do is beg&quot; -Nix<br /> <br /> &quot;There's thing about being a vampire, Frank; it takes a long fucking time to learn how do all the cool shit&quot;. -Abigail","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2521-iguazu","name":"Iguazu","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2521_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"740"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-03T16:11:47-07:00","id":1517114,"title":"","content":"An intriguing idea but I think at this point I would rather explore the isolation Requiem builds into the setting for each city of kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3761-yab","name":"Yab","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"81"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2023-07-04T05:21:45-07:00","id":1517153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>HaintBleu</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/1516376-new-orleans-or-chicago?p=1516604#post1516604\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">With New Orlean's reputation for hauntings and the Louisiana folklore of the rougarou, New Orleans has ready built hooks for Geist and Werewolf crossovers, besides the existing Vampire material.</div> </div> </div> </div>Room for some mix &amp; match even since the Rougarou, like many other legendary critters when relocated from their places of origin, seems to suffer some degree of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rougarou#American_folklore\" target=\"_blank\">memetic mutation</a> so to speak. Human body with the head of a wolf or dog could be an Uratha, or some underworld native resembling Anubis, for example.<br /> <br /> Beside this, there's the occasional association with witchcraft as a source of the transformation, what brings to mind the similarly named <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soucouyant\" target=\"_blank\">Loogaroo</a> from caribbean folklore, and in itself can rise some <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marinette_(loa)\" target=\"_blank\">other associations</a>....<br /> <br /> Marinette being a Loa makes for a - somewhat flimsy, since she's particular from Haitian Voodoo, not <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Louisiana_Voodoo\" target=\"_blank\">Louisiana</a>'s - possible hook to Baron Cimitiere or other hougans &amp; mambos in the region, while her representation as a screech owl along penchant for violent/harmful possession bring some heavy Strix tones to mind. The link to werewolves could deal with Uratha proper, a number of less known wolf/dog-seeming\u200b spirits or supernatural beings, such as the Beasts of Bethlehem from the 1e Antagonists blue book or some sort of Synthesis shenanigans.<br /> <br /> Just some rambling, spur-of-moment thoughts to throw into the mix.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1147,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","user":"Baaldam","date":". 07-04-2023, 09:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}